1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,654
JAKE:

2
00:00:02,654 --> 00:00:05,630
Hello, Junior Cycle camp, Jake speaking.

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,117
WOMAN:

4
00:00:07,117 --> 00:00:07,198
Hi.

5
00:00:07,198 --> 00:00:12,918
I'm calling for some information about the cycle camp – I'm thinking of sending

6
00:00:12,918 --> 00:00:13,890
my son.

7
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:13,940
JAKE:

8
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:14,967
Great.

9
00:00:14,967 --> 00:00:24,123
Well, it's held every weekday morning over the summer vacation and we focus on basic cycling skills

10
00:00:24,123 --> 00:00:25,200
and safety.

11
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:31,000
We have eight levels for children from three years upwards.

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,280
How old's your son?

13
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:33,862
WOMAN:

14
00:00:33,862 --> 00:00:34,445
Charlie?

15
00:00:34,445 --> 00:00:35,610
He's seven.

16
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:37,492
He can ride a bike,

17
00:00:37,492 --> 00:00:42,764
but he needs a little more training before he's safe to go on the

18
00:00:42,764 --> 00:00:43,140
road.

19
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:43,611
JAKE:

20
00:00:43,611 --> 00:00:46,910
He'd probably be best in Level 5.

21
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:50,448
They start off practising on the site here,

22
00:00:50,448 --> 00:00:54,871
and we aim to get them riding on the road,

23
00:00:54,871 --> 00:01:00,620
but first they're taken to ride in the park, away from the traffic.

24
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:01,104
WOMAN:

25
00:01:01,104 --> 00:01:01,588
Right.

26
00:01:01,588 --> 00:01:06,430
And can you tell me a bit about the instructors?

27
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:07,049
JAKE:

28
00:01:07,049 --> 00:01:12,000
Well, all our staff wear different coloured shirts.

29
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,255
So, we have three supervisors,

30
00:01:14,255 --> 00:01:16,510
and they have red shirts.

31
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:18,425
They support the instructors,

32
00:01:18,425 --> 00:01:23,690
and they also stand in for me if I'm not around.

33
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:28,584
Then the instructors themselves are in blue shirts,

34
00:01:28,584 --> 00:01:34,090
and one of these is responsible for each class.

35
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:34,715
WOMAN:

36
00:01:34,715 --> 00:01:35,340
OK.

37
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:35,891
JAKE:

38
00:01:35,891 --> 00:01:43,600
In order to be accepted, all our instructors have to submit a reference from

39
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:50,758
someone who's seen them work with children – like if they've worked as a

40
00:01:50,758 --> 00:01:52,410
babysitter, for example.

41
00:01:52,410 --> 00:01:59,022
Then they have to complete our training course, including how to do lesson plans,

42
00:01:59,022 --> 00:02:04,690
and generally care for the well-being of the kids in their class.

43
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:08,000
They do a great job, I have to say.

44
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,500
WOMAN:

45
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:09,000
Right.

46
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
And tell me a bit about the classes.

47
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,350
What size will Charlie's class be?

48
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:16,826
JAKE:

49
00:02:16,826 --> 00:02:21,580
We have a limit of eight children in each class,

50
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:25,860
so their instructor really gets to know them well.

51
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:32,176
They're out riding most of the time but they have quiet times too, where

52
00:02:32,176 --> 00:02:38,491
their instructor might tell them a story that's got something to do with cycling,

53
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:42,100
or get them to play a game together.

54
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,830
It's a lot of fun.

55
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:44,429
WOMAN:

56
00:02:44,429 --> 00:02:46,226
It must be.

57
00:02:46,226 --> 00:02:49,820
Now, what happens if there's rain?

58
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,450
Do the classes still run?

59
00:02:52,450 --> 00:02:52,893
JAKE:

60
00:02:52,893 --> 00:02:53,778
Oh yes.

61
00:02:53,778 --> 00:02:59,532
We don't let that put us off – we just put on our waterproofs

62
00:02:59,532 --> 00:03:00,860
and keep cycling.

63
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:01,568
WOMAN:

64
00:03:01,568 --> 00:03:09,360
And is there anything special Charlie should bring along with him?

65
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:09,903
JAKE:

66
00:03:09,903 --> 00:03:16,420
Well, maybe some spare clothes, especially if the weather's not so good.

67
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:20,230
And a snack for break time.

68
00:03:20,230 --> 00:03:20,854
WOMAN:

69
00:03:20,854 --> 00:03:23,350
How about a drink?

70
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:23,634
JAKE:

71
00:03:23,634 --> 00:03:24,770
No, we'll provide that.

72
00:03:24,770 --> 00:03:29,070
And make sure he has shoes, not sandals.

73
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:29,601
WOMAN:

74
00:03:29,601 --> 00:03:30,132
Sure.

75
00:03:30,132 --> 00:03:36,503
And just at present Charlie has to take medication every few hours,

76
00:03:36,503 --> 00:03:40,220
so I'll make sure he has that.

77
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:40,658
JAKE:

78
00:03:40,658 --> 00:03:41,097
Absolutely.

79
00:03:41,097 --> 00:03:45,919
Just give us details of when he has to take it

80
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:48,550
and we'll make sure he does.

81
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:49,095
WOMAN:

82
00:03:49,095 --> 00:03:49,640
Thanks.

83
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,024
JAKE:

84
00:03:50,024 --> 00:03:55,396
Now, there are a few things you should know about Day 1 of the

85
00:03:55,396 --> 00:03:55,780
camp.

86
00:03:55,780 --> 00:04:00,178
The classes normally start at 9.30 every morning,

87
00:04:00,178 --> 00:04:07,020
but on Day 1 you should aim to get Charlie here by 9.20.

88
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:12,360
The finishing time will be 12.30 as usual.

89
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:19,170
We need the additional time because there are a few extra things to do.

90
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:26,464
The most important is that we have a very careful check to make sure

91
00:04:26,464 --> 00:04:29,590
that every child's helmet fits properly.

92
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:33,300
If it doesn't fit, we'll try to adjust it,

93
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:38,659
or we'll find him another one – but he must wear it all the

94
00:04:38,659 --> 00:04:40,720
time he's on the bike.

95
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:41,283
WOMAN:

96
00:04:41,283 --> 00:04:42,410
Of course.

97
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:42,853
JAKE:

98
00:04:42,853 --> 00:04:48,609
Then after that, all the instructors will be waiting to meet their classes,

99
00:04:48,609 --> 00:04:53,480
and they'll meet up in the tent – you can't miss it.

100
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:59,100
And each instructor will take their class away and get started.

101
00:04:59,100 --> 00:04:59,704
WOMAN:

102
00:04:59,704 --> 00:05:00,309
OK.

103
00:05:00,309 --> 00:05:03,330
Well that all sounds good.

104
00:05:03,330 --> 00:05:09,090
Now can you tell me how much the camp costs a week?

105
00:05:09,090 --> 00:05:09,838
JAKE:

106
00:05:09,838 --> 00:05:12,830
One hundred ninety-nine dollars.

107
00:05:12,830 --> 00:05:18,899
We've managed to keep the price more or less the same as last year

108
00:05:18,899 --> 00:05:21,500
– it was one hundred ninety then.

109
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:25,680
But the places are filling up quite quickly.

110
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,271
WOMAN:

111
00:05:26,271 --> 00:05:26,862
Right.

112
00:05:26,862 --> 00:05:31,000
OK, well I'd like to book for …
